  "quant_evidence:humans& The 4-bitter Lesson:NVFP4 前向 + BF16 反向：用原始 BF16 值（high_preci.value": "high_precision computes the gradient of the unquantized function and has occasional gradient spikes; dequantized gradients correspond to the function actually executed, with far fewer large spikes under Adam; using only two of 4/6, dequantized backward, and BF16 for the last 15% of layers still gives spikes; with all three, gradient norms are stable across 5 runs and reward tracks BF16",
  "quant_evidence:humans& The 4-bitter Lesson:4/6 用在 RL 的权重和激活上（原论文只用于预训练激活）.hw": "Not stated",
  "quant_evidence:humans& The 4-bitter Lesson:4/6 用在 RL 的权重和激活上（原论文只用于预训练激活）.claim": "4/6 applied to RL weights and activations (the original paper used it only for pretraining activations)",
  "quant_evidence:humans& The 4-bitter Lesson:4/6 用在 RL 的权重和激活上（原论文只用于预训练激活）.value": "Each block picks whichever of amax→6 and amax→4 has the smaller error; fused into the quantization kernel, with no noticeable increase in rollout time; reference KL is clearly more stable; the TE and FlashInfer sides are bitwise identical, including error accumulation and comparison",
